==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*3 [[Haterbaa 2.0]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 6.67~16.67 seconds<sup>200f~500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Samurai Doggy]] spawns as the boss.
**15 [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**4 [[Haterbaa 2.0]]s spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Make sure to bring [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitters]] for the first part, like [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Jurassic Cat]] or [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catornado]], so the HaterBaa 2.0s are not a problem. Since Samurai Doggy is both a [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemy and a [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] enemy, either type of Cat Unit is useful against him here. You could use any form of [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Weightlifter Cat]] or [[Swordsman Cat (Rare Cat)|Swordsman Cat]] to deal [[Massive Damage|massive damage]] against them. You may also want to bring some ranged units, such as [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Gross Cat]] or [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], to take out the Trolly Bloggers. Other than that, there isn't much else to the stage.

==Trivia==
*"No Right Swipes" refers to the dating app Tinder, in which swiping right is a way to show your approval of someone after seeing their profile.

